msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of years
#: src/Privacy/Privacy.php:237
#, php-format
msgid ""
"When a customer enters a VAT number at checkout, we check it with the official registry for its country: VIES (European Commission) for EU numbers, and HMRC (UK), the Swiss UID register or the Brønnøysund Register (Norway) for those countries. The registry receives the VAT number and, for VIES, our own VAT number as the requester. The registry returns whether the number is valid and, where it publishes them, the registered name and address.\n"
"\n"
"We store the VAT number, the registry result including that name and address and the consultation number, and the country of the customer's IP address with the order. We use the IP country, together with the billing and shipping country, as evidence of where the sale takes place. Registry results are also cached for a short period.\n"
"\n"
"EU VAT rules require us to keep these records for %d years after the end of the year of the sale. Within that period a request to erase them cannot be met, and we keep only what the VAT records need. After that period the VAT number, registered name and address, consultation number and IP country are removed from the order and the VAT ledger automatically."
msgstr ""

